Q: gcc 13.3.0: [-Wstringop-overflow=] A: <p>This is a well-known and confusing GCC warning.</p>
<p>The <code>st_size</code> field of the <code>stat</code> structure is typically of type <code>off_t</code>, a signed integer type. It can store negative values that become huge unsigned values that exceed <code>PTRDIFF_MAX</code>. GCC tries to warn about that. The suppression is simple, compare the value against the constant:</p>
<pre><code>if (0 &lt;= fi.st_size &amp;&amp; fi.st_size &lt; PTRDIFF_MAX) {
  htt = calloc(1, fi.st_size + 1);
  r = read(fd, htt, fi.st_size);
}
</code></pre>
